---
/**
 * The emotional center of the page. Condensed from the Guild's own Case for
 * Support. No detail here is invented.
 */
import Section from '@/components/ui/Section.astro';
import Picture from '@/components/ui/Picture.astro';
---

<Section tone="paper" labelledby="story-title">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[2fr_3fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-8 lg:self-start">
      <Picture slot="foundingStory" sizes="(min-width: 64rem) 35vw, 100vw" aspect="4 / 3" />
      <blockquote class="mt-6 max-w-[40ch] font-serif italic leading-relaxed text-ash">
        <p>
          “All these are skilled with their hands, each one an expert at his own work. Without them
          no city could be lived in… Yet they maintain the fabric of the world.”
        </p>
        <footer class="mt-2 font-sans text-[0.9rem] not-italic">Sirach 38:31–34</footer>
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <div class="measure flex flex-col gap-5 font-serif text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.7] md:text-[1.125rem]">
      <h2 id="story-title" class="text-h2 font-sans">
        Our Story
      </h2>
      <p>
        It began with one plumber, one van, and the Lord as his only companion. Years of small jobs
        in the basements of nearly invisible people brought him face to face with the working poor,
        not as customers but as children of God. When the bill came, he saw the anxiety in their
        faces. So he did what he could: a discount here, a free repair there.
      </p>
      <p>
        One client he never forgot: an elderly woman in a wheelchair, alone on a fixed income in a
        weathered house on the backroads of Missouri. When he finished, she asked him to do more.
        She could not afford anyone else. She had no one else to ask. If not him, then who?
      </p>
      <p>
        Then a friend from church, newly in business himself, began partnering with him. Then
        another Catholic tradesman joined. Then another. They prayed before each job, traded labor,
        and showed up when a brother was in need. A handful of men living their faith at work had
        become a brotherhood.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
